.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OPENSSL_LH_STATS 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OPENSSL_LH_stats ,
.Nm OPENSSL_LH_node_stats ,
.Nm OPENSSL_LH_node_usage_stats ,
.Nm OPENSSL_LH_stats_bio ,
.Nm OPENSSL_LH_node_stats_bio ,
.Nm OPENSSL_LH_node_usage_stats_bio
.Nd LHASH statistics
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/lhash.h
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.1, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft void
.Fo OPENSSL_LH_node_stats
.Fa "LHASH *table"
.Fa "FILE *out"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo OPENSSL_LH_node_usage_stats
.Fa "LHASH *table"
.Fa "FILE *out"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo OPENSSL_LH_node_stats_bio
.Fa "LHASH *table"
.Fa "BIO *out"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo OPENSSL_LH_node_usage_stats_bio
.Fa "LHASH *table"
.Fa "BIO *out"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo OPENSSL_LH_stats
.Fa "LHASH *table"
.Fa "FILE *out"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo OPENSSL_LH_stats_bio
.Fa "LHASH *table"
.Fa "BIO *out"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Vt LHASH
structure records statistics about most aspects of accessing the hash
table.
.Pp
.Fn OPENSSL_LH_stats
prints out statistics on the size of the hash table and how many entries
are in it.
For historical reasons, this function also outputs a number of
additional statistics, but the tracking of these statistics is no longer
supported and these statistics are always reported as zero.
.Pp
.Fn OPENSSL_LH_node_stats
prints the number of entries for each 'bucket' in the hash table.
.Pp
.Fn OPENSSL_LH_node_usage_stats
prints out a short summary of the state of the hash table.
It prints the 'load' and the 'actual load'.
The load is the average number of data items per 'bucket' in the hash
table.
The 'actual load' is the average number of items per 'bucket', but only
for buckets which contain entries.
So the 'actual load' is the average number of searches that will need to
find an item in the hash table, while the 'load' is the average number
that will be done to record a miss.
.Pp
.Fn OPENSSL_LH_stats_bio ,
.Fn OPENSSL_LH_node_stats_bio
and
.Fn OPENSSL_LH_node_usage_stats_bio
are the same as the above, except that the output goes to a
.Vt BIO .
.Pp
These functions are deprecated and should no longer be used.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions do not return values.
.Sh NOTE
These calls should be made under a read lock.
Refer to
.Xr OPENSSL_LH_COMPFUNC 3
for more details about the locks required when using the LHASH data
structure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bio 7 ,
.Xr OPENSSL_LH_COMPFUNC 3
.Sh HISTORY
These functions were deprecated in version 3.1.
